  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "電影與文學",
    "sub_ename": "FILM AND LITERATURE",
    "describe_ch": "電影與文學課程藉由學習西方文化的神話故事增進語文能力。透過閱讀、分析傳統古希臘神話及聖經故事來審視現代文本中不斷出現的傳統文學主題。本課程帶領學生研讀簡易版的神話故事與經典文學名著，進而探索文學在音樂、電影、及網路現象之詮釋。並強調發展批判及創意思考之能力。",
    "describe_eh": " Film and Literature is a class designed to help the students learn about western culture from some of its earliest myths. We will study creation myths from ancient Greece and the Bible, and see how the underlying, fundamental themes are repeated in modern cultural texts. The structure of the learning will be to move from simplified versions of the original myths through simplified versions found in classic English literature to contemporary renditions in music, film and online phenomenon. It is a knowledge based course with an emphasis on the development of critical and creative thinking skills.",
